am last season.","published":"2026-01-02T17:59:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/47482708/notre-dame-wr-jordan-faison-play-lacrosse-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Notre Dame's Jordan Faison to miss 1-2 weeks with ankle injury","description":"Notre Dame starting wide receiver Jordan Faison suffered a sprained right ankle against Texas A&M and will miss one to two weeks.","published":"2024-09-03T01:37:46.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/41097668/notre-dame-jordan-faison-miss-1-2-weeks-ankle-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"SEC standardized NIL, revenue sharing contracts 'unfair' for players, agents say","description":"The SEC's new uniform NIL and revenue sharing agreements are causing an uproar among agents concerned that the contracts are loaded with terms that are unfair.","published":"2026-11-20T01:16:03.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50535591/sec-standardized-nil-contracts-unfair-players-agents-say","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Waiver approved allowing Army, Navy to play 13th game in 2027","description":"The waiver will allow Army and Navy to play 12 games apiece before the College Football Playoff selections are made and keep their rivalry game.","published":"2026-11-19T23:50:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50535192/waiver-approved-army-navy-13th-game-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"James Madison moving to American Conference in 2027","description":"James Madison is leaving the Sun Belt Conference for the American Conference a year earlier than planned, in 2027 rather than 2028.","published":"2026-11-19T21:30:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50534149/james-madison-moving-american-conference-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft Big Board rankings: Mel Kiper's top 25 prospects, best by position","description":"Six quarterbacks and six receivers ranked in the top 25? Mel Kiper Jr. stacks the best players on the 2027 draft board as of mid-November.","published":"2026-11-19T22:42:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50182998/2027-nfl-draft-rankings-kiper-big-board-top-prospects","type":"Story","byline":"Mel Kiper Jr.","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Michigan WR Andrew Marsh facing misdemeanor indecent exposure charge","description":"Michigan receiver Andrew Marsh is facing a misdemeanor charge of indecent exposure stemming from a February incident involving a food service driver.","published":"2026-11-19T21:15:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50533990/michigan-wr-marsh-facing-misdemeanor-indecent-exposure-charge","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Which teams have the best odds to make the College Football Playoff?","description":"We are tracking the odds for making the CFP, earning a bye and winning it all.","published":"2026-11-19T21:22:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Hall of Famer Jack Ham returning to broadcast booth after health scare","description":"Hall of Fame linebacker and Penn State radio analyst Jack Ham will return to the broadcast booth on Saturday, just two weeks after suffering a medical emergency.","published":"2026-11-19T19:37:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532925/jack-ham-returning-broadcast-booth-health-scare","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 'College GameDay' Week 12: Virginia Tech vs. Miami","description":"\"College GameDay\" heads to University of Miami for Week 12.","published":"2026-11-19T19:27:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532540/2026-college-gameday-week-12-virginia-tech-vs-miami","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5150424/jordan-faison","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan_Faison"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jordan Faison","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan_Faison","description":"American football and lacrosse player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:20Z","intro":"Quincy Jordan Faison II (born April 7, 2004) is an American college football wide receiver for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish. He previously also played midfielder for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish lacrosse team.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Faison grew up in Weston, Florida and attended the Pine Crest School, where he played basketball, lacrosse, and football. In football, he played safety and quarterback in Pine Crest's Wing T offense and accumulated 1,800 all-purpose yards and scored 26 total touchdowns as a senior. Faison was a three-time All-American in lacrosse."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Faison entered his freshman football season at Notre Dame as a walk-on before earning a football scholarship midway through the season. He was named the MVP of the 2023 Sun Bowl after catching five passes for 115 yards and a touchdown in a 48–8 win over Oregon State. Faison finished his freshman football season with 19 receptions for 322 yards and four touchdowns.\nFaison was a starting midfielder in his freshman season with the Notre Dame Fighting Irish men's lacrosse team and scored 22 goals. He scored a goal in Notre Dame's 15–5 victory in the 2024 National Championship game against Maryland. He retired from lacrosse in January 2026 to focus fully on football."}]}}